The expanded value is inverted, and the state belongs on the controlling button. Use aria-expanded={!isCollapsed} on that button and connect it to the panel with aria-controls.

```jsx
function Section({ open, onToggle, buttonId, panelId, label, children }) {
  return (
    <section>
      <h3><button type="button" id={buttonId}
        aria-expanded={open} aria-controls={panelId}
        onClick={onToggle}>{label}</button></h3>
      <div id={panelId} hidden={!open}>{children}</div>
    </section>
  );
}
```

The parent supplies unique IDs and toggles open. This example is one accordion section; multi-section policy belongs to its parent.

**Check:** When open is false, the panel is hidden and the button reports false. Toggle once and verify both switch together.

